# ⚠️ The gitlink for nats.zig existed before this file did, which meant a fresh clone got an
# empty `nats.zig/` directory and no way to populate it: git recorded the commit but had no
# URL to fetch it from. `git submodule update --init` failed with "No url found for submodule
# path 'nats.zig'".
#
# The URL is UPSTREAM, not a fork — local fixes to this submodule cannot be pushed here.
# They live in the parent repo as `nats.zig-*.patch` plus NATS_ZIG_NOTES.md, so they survive
# independently of the submodule and are ready to send upstream. Re-apply with:
#
#     cd nats.zig && git apply ../nats.zig-jetstream-stale-408.patch
[submodule "nats.zig"]
	path = nats.zig
	url = https://github.com/lalinsky/nats.zig.git
	branch = main
